FLOW 6 -- Client queries historical metrics (Flux query against InfluxDB)
============================================================
[operator] curl "/api/v1/metrics/history?broker_id=broker-1&from=2026-08-10T00:00:00Z"
                 -H "x-api-key: ..."

--- gateway side ---
[gateway/main.rs] require_api_key -- key matches: PASS
[gateway/main.rs] GovernorLayer -- under rate limit: PASS
[gateway/main.rs] proxy() -- OriginalUri = "/api/v1/metrics/history?broker_id=..."
                 forwarded_path = strip_prefix("/api/v1") -> "/metrics/history?..."
                 target = "http://agent:3000/metrics/history?broker_id=..."
[gateway/main.rs] reqwest::Client -- GET request sent, method/query/body preserved

--- agent side: validation before touching InfluxDB ---
[http.rs | get_metrics_history()] Query<HistoryQuery> extracted
                 -- broker_id="broker-1", from="2026-08-10T00:00:00Z", to=None
[http.rs] chrono::DateTime::parse_from_rfc3339(&q.from) -- valid RFC3339: PASS
[http.rs] config::is_valid_id(&q.broker_id) -- "broker-1" matches
                 alphanumeric/_/- charset: PASS
                 -- this check exists specifically because broker_id gets
                    interpolated directly into the Flux query string below;
                    it's the mitigation for that injection risk noted in
                    the code comments
[http.rs] q.to is None -> defaulted to Utc::now().to_rfc3339()
[http.rs] chrono::DateTime::parse_from_rfc3339(&to) -- valid: PASS
[http.rs] limit = q.limit.unwrap_or(100).min(1000) -- no limit given -> 100
[http.rs] offset = q.offset.unwrap_or(0) -- 0

--- building and running the Flux query ---
[http.rs] format!() -- built Flux string:
    from(bucket: "broker-metrics")
      |> range(start: 2026-08-10T00:00:00Z, stop: 2026-08-17T14:02:00Z)
      |> filter(fn: (r) => r._measurement == "broker_metrics")
      |> filter(fn: (r) => r.broker_id == "broker-1")
      |> pivot(rowKey: ["_time"], columnKey: ["_field"], valueColumn: "_value")
      |> sort(columns: ["_time"], desc: false)
      |> limit(n: 100, offset: 0)

[http.rs] influxdb2::models::Query::new(flux)
[http.rs] state.influx_client.query::<BrokerMetricsHistory>(Some(query))
[influxdb2 crate] HTTP POST to InfluxDB's /api/v2/query endpoint
[influxdb] executed Flux script -- 47 rows matched the range + filters
[influxdb2 crate] deserialized rows into Vec<BrokerMetricsHistory> via
                 the #[derive(FromDataPoint)] on that struct
                 -- NOTE: this struct does NOT have net_rx_bytes,
                    net_tx_bytes, mqtt_online, docker_online fields --
                    those exist on the LIVE BrokerMetricsResponse but were
                    never written by influx.rs, so history queries can
                    never return them even though the API shape suggests
                    they might

[http.rs] Ok(results) branch -- count = 47
[http.rs] built HistoryEnvelope{ broker_id, from, to, limit, offset, count, results }
[http.rs] returned 200 OK with JSON body

--- back through the gateway ---
[gateway/main.rs | proxy()] upstream response received, status=200
                 content_type copied from agent's response
                 bytes streamed back unmodified to the original caller
[operator] receives HistoryEnvelope{ count: 47, results: [...] } as JSON
    -> 47 historical points delivered, scoped to exactly one broker and
       one time range, never touching the raw InfluxDB port directly
       (InfluxDB itself is never published to the host -- only reachable
       from the agent, same internal-only pattern as the agent itself)

--- contrast: what happens if broker_id fails validation ---
[operator] curl ".../metrics/history?broker_id=broker-1;DROP+MEASUREMENT&from=..."
[http.rs | get_metrics_history()] config::is_valid_id() -- semicolon not in
                 allowed charset: FAIL
[http.rs] returned 400 Bad Request { error: "invalid broker_id" }
    -> query never reaches the format!() call at all -- the malformed
       broker_id is rejected before it could be interpolated into Flux
